    "understanding": "updated",
    "rationale": "Next compare async storage completion across term changes with safe-read support across configuration changes. The storage path has explicit term and entry-identity protections and a directly controllable ordered-worker boundary, making legal same-history checks feasible. ReadIndex/configuration has potentially wider read-safety consequences but first needs producer/consumer decomposition and an applicable request contract. Synchronous ordering reconciliation is a narrower interface discriminator that changes harness legality; retain both statements rather than silently choosing one. Prefer expanding the async completion producer/consumer map and checking a delayed old completion plus a fresh completion under a legal RawNode history.",
